<%#
  ONE OF THE PROJECT FOLDER'S SUBFOLDERS, AS A PANEL ON A VISITOR'S PAGE (2026-09-08, folder
  panels; spec §5). The maker's own page renders the same folder through projects/_folder_panel
  with tiles, list or the Finder browser and a toggle to change it; this one is READ-ONLY — there
  is nothing here to post to, and the view is whatever the maker chose.

  A VISITOR GETS A LIST WHERE THE MAKER CHOSE THE BROWSER (spec decision 7). The Miller-columns
  browser reads LibraryBrowseController#children, which is session-authed and answers in the
  SIGNED-IN user's library — a visitor has none, so mounting it here would be a panel that fetches
  a 404 forever. A public children endpoint is a separate design; until it exists, `browser` reads
  as the list, which shows the same files with the same links. That is why the branch below asks
  only whether the view is `tiles`.

  NESTED FOLDERS ARE SUB-HEADINGS, NOT PANELS (spec decision 3): depth one is a panel and
  everything under it renders inside its parent, which is `pub.folder_sections`' walk — the dir's
  own files first with no heading (the panel head already names the folder), then each nested
  subfolder that holds files, labelled relative to THIS folder.

  AN EMPTY FOLDER IS OMITTED, unlike the maker's own quiet panel: an empty heading on a public page
  invites the reader to add the first file, which is the one thing a visitor cannot do (S3-4's
  rule, stated in public/projects/_page.html.erb's header).

  Locals: pub (Maker::PublicProject), key (the layout key, "folder:<node_id>"), dir
  (Maker::ProjectFolderListing::Dir), view (one of Maker::Project::VIEWS).
%>
<% sections = pub.folder_sections(dir) %>
<% if sections.any? %>
  <section class="panel folder-panel" id="<%= key %>">
    <div class="panel-head">
      <h2><%= dir.name %></h2>
      <%# THE WHOLE SUBTREE, matching what this panel renders — Dir#subtree_file_count, the same
          number the maker's panel head shows. This dir's own files alone would read "(1)" over a
          folder whose nested sections list twenty. %>
      <span class="mono muted"><%= pluralize(dir.subtree_file_count, "file") %></span>
    </div>

    <% sections.each do |name, rows| %>
      <% if name %>
        <h3 class="public-section"><%= name %></h3>
      <% end %>
      <% if view == "tiles" %>
        <div class="public-tiles">
          <% rows.each do |row| %>
            <%# THE FILE'S OWN PAGE, never its bytes — the same answer _files.html.erb's name cell
                and _photos.html.erb's picture give: a visitor clicking a tile wants to LOOK at the
                file, and that page carries the viewer and the Download button both.
                `pub.preview_url_for` is the thumbnail's URL and the ONLY spelling allowed here: a
                blob URL is unauthenticated and never expires (tinkerex#278, the seam guard's third
                arm), so files/_thumb takes it as a strict local. %>
            <% ext = File.extname(row.node.name).delete(".").upcase.first(4) %>
            <%= link_to pub.view_url_for(row.node_id), class: "grid-card file-cell",
                        title: row.node.name do %>
              <%= render "files/thumb", thumb: pub.thumbs.thumb(row.node_id), ext_label: ext,
                         url: pub.preview_url_for(row.node_id) %>
              <span class="grid-name"><%= row.node.name %></span>
            <% end %>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      <% else %>
        <%# `list` AND `browser` BOTH LAND HERE — the header says why the browser cannot mount for a
            visitor. The four cells are the same ones public/projects/_files draws for the root. %>
        <table class="table public-files">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th class="col-thumb"></th>
              <th class="col-name">File</th>
              <th class="col-size">Size</th>
              <th class="col-dl"></th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <% rows.each do |row| %>
              <% ext = File.extname(row.node.name).delete(".").upcase %>
              <tr>
                <td class="col-thumb">
                  <span class="file-cell">
                    <%= render "files/thumb", thumb: pub.thumbs.thumb(row.node_id), ext_label: ext,
                               url: pub.preview_url_for(row.node_id) %>
                  </span>
                </td>
                <td class="col-name"><%= link_to row.node.name, pub.view_url_for(row.node_id) %></td>
                <td class="col-size num"><%= number_to_human_size(row.node.size) %></td>
                <td class="col-dl">
                  <%= link_to "Download", pub.file_url_for(row.node_id, download: true), class: "linkbtn small" %>
                </td>
              </tr>
            <% end %>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  </section>
<% end %>
